From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:33:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/options: Set the stream group type after allocating
 its parameters

The fix is one of the two recommended in the report.

Fixes: NULL pointer dereference
Fixes: Ks5s2XRvqzXe
Fixes: AISLE-2026-0111-00423
NULL pointer dereference Replicated through UnModified FFprobe with an allocation failure injected by gdb
Found-by: Joshua Rogers <joshua.rogers@aisle.com>
---
 libavformat/options.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/options.c b/libavformat/options.c
index abdabca15f..df7b6434d8 100644
--- a/libavformat/options.c
+++ b/libavformat/options.c
@@ -490,7 +490,6 @@ AVStreamGroup *avformat_stream_group_create(AVFormatContext *s,
 
     stg->av_class = &stream_group_class;
     av_opt_set_defaults(stg);
-    stg->type = type;
     switch (type) {
     case AV_STREAM_GROUP_PARAMS_IAMF_AUDIO_ELEMENT:
         stg->params.iamf_audio_element = av_iamf_audio_element_alloc();
@@ -528,6 +527,7 @@ AVStreamGroup *avformat_stream_group_create(AVFormatContext *s,
     default:
         goto fail;
     }
+    stg->type = type;
 
     if (options) {
         if (av_opt_set_dict2(stg, options, AV_OPT_SEARCH_CHILDREN))
-- 
2.56.0

